   [
    "Parameterized named types continue to be considered identical (as reported by the `Identical` function) if they satisfy pointer equality.",
    "Instantiated named types are considered identical if their origin types are identical and their type arguments are pairwise identical.",
    "Instantiating twice with the same origin type and type arguments _may_ result in pointer-identical `*Named` instances, but this is not guaranteed.",
    "There is further discussion of this in the [instantiation](#instantiation) section below."
   ]
  ]
 },
