    "The `command/resolve` request is sent from the client to the server to check whether a command is ready for execution or requires additional user input.",
    "Before executing any command that supports interactive resolution, the client must call `command/resolve` at least once to determine if the command arguments are comprehensive.",
    "As long as the `ExecuteCommandParams` contains non-empty `formFields` (questions), the client should not execute the command.",
    "Instead, the client should collect the user's answers and call `command/resolve` with the answers populated in `formAnswers`."
   ]
  ]
 },
